Training data (of AksharSTT v4, and of this model's own training run)
  IndicVoices (Hindi), AI4Bharat, CC-BY-4.0: https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/IndicVoices
  Vaani, transcribed part (Hindi), ARTPARK and the Indian Institute of Science, CC-BY-4.0:
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/ARTPARK-IISc/Vaani-transcription-part
  Shrutilipi (Hindi), AI4Bharat, from All India Radio news bulletins, CC-BY-4.0:
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/Shrutilipi
    Part of it was transcribed by Shruti, and part by an earlier internal akshar model (v2), kept only where
    that transcript agrees with the bulletin's script.
  Kathbath (Hindi), AI4Bharat, CC-BY-4.0: https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/Kathbath
  Rural Women ASR v2 (Hindi), AI4Bharat, CC-BY-4.0: https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/Rural_Women_ASR_v2
  FLEURS (Hindi train split), Google, CC-BY-4.0: https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs
  NPTEL (English and Hindi lectures), AI4Bharat, from NPTEL course lectures, CC-BY-4.0:
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/NPTEL
  LibriSpeech (train-clean-100 and train-clean-360), Vassil Panayotov, Guoguo Chen, Daniel Povey and
    Sanjeev Khudanpur, CC-BY-4.0: https://www.openslr.org/12
  MUCS 2021 Hindi-English code-switching data (training split), from the MUCS 2021 challenge, CC-BY-SA-4.0:
    https://www.openslr.org/104 (copy used: https://huggingface.co/datasets/dianavdavidson/MUCS-Hinglish)
  Common Voice Scripted Speech 26.0, South Asian English, and Common Voice 27.0, Hindi, Mozilla Foundation and
    its contributors, CC0-1.0, obtained under the Mozilla Data Collective terms:
    https://datacollective.mozillafoundation.org/
    Those terms ask that outputs of models built with the data be disclosed to downstream users as
    machine-generated.
  Silence and noise clips generated by akshar's own code

English-word list
  A curated list of 2,900 English words, brands and place names with their Devanagari spellings, made by the
  akshar project. It decides which words the training transcripts write in Latin letters.
  data/english-words in https://github.com/byteknotlabsai/akshar

